1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,740
[CHAPTER.3]
[Take the first step, and the heavens will follow]

2
00:00:04,699 --> 00:00:05,931
[Egypt Trip DAY 2]

3
00:00:05,932 --> 00:00:07,865
[EGYPT DAY 2]

4
00:00:08,366 --> 00:00:12,033
[Good morning!]

5
00:00:12,034 --> 00:00:13,567
[Is it really a good morning...?]

6
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:16,532
[Same morning, different fate]

7
00:00:16,532 --> 00:00:18,499
[In the desert morning,]

8
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,032
[one lone tent flaps in the wind]

9
00:00:23,132 --> 00:00:26,432
[The sound of coughing
wakes the desert]

10
00:00:28,186 --> 00:00:28,966
Ugh, it's so cold.

11
00:00:28,966 --> 00:00:30,899
[Only a sleeping bag to keep warm...]

12
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,791
Oh, my back is killing me…

13
00:00:33,792 --> 00:00:35,698
[The 44-year-old leader
whose back hurts from sleeping on the floor]

14
00:00:35,699 --> 00:00:36,632
Ugh…

15
00:00:36,891 --> 00:00:37,701
Agh…

16
00:00:38,366 --> 00:00:41,139
[One by one, they wake up]

17
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:42,477
How long did we even sleep?

18
00:00:43,559 --> 00:00:45,813
[Our pauper leader's feeling homesick]
I want to go home.

19
00:00:45,814 --> 00:00:47,366
I want to go home.

20
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:49,795
[His complaints intensified overnight]
Take me home.

21
00:00:49,796 --> 00:00:50,833
Ugh, my back hurts.

22
00:00:51,199 --> 00:00:53,266
At least we're still alive…

23
00:00:54,032 --> 00:00:55,098
[Thankfully, the paupers
made it through the night]

24
00:00:55,099 --> 00:00:56,932
Are we seriously stranded here?

25
00:00:57,469 --> 00:00:59,998
The moment we opened
our eyes in the morning,

26
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:01,999
the sandy winds woke us up.

27
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,579
The sand was our blankets.

28
00:01:03,587 --> 00:01:06,073
[Pauper-exclusive sand blankets & sand alarm clock]
And the sandy wind was our alarm clock.

29
00:01:06,832 --> 00:01:09,399
[Meanwhile, morning also arrives
at the princes' accommodation]

30
00:01:10,059 --> 00:01:12,932
[Here's your breakfast, Your Highness]
Come in.

31
00:01:13,203 --> 00:01:14,099
Oh!

32
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:16,799
[Breakfast room service to enjoy in comfort]
Welcome!

33
00:01:17,266 --> 00:01:18,366
Would you like it outside?

34
00:01:18,737 --> 00:01:20,532
[The terrace is perfect]
It'd be great out there. Okay!

35
00:01:21,466 --> 00:01:23,266
I swung open the terrace door
and stepped out…

36
00:01:23,267 --> 00:01:24,407
Gasp!

37
00:01:25,189 --> 00:01:27,332
[The pyramid view that took the prince's breath away]
The pyramid was right in front of my eyes!

38
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:28,588
It was literally just there.

39
00:01:28,966 --> 00:01:30,499
It was so beautiful.

40
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,066
It was a spectacular sight.

41
00:01:34,099 --> 00:01:36,166
[DAWN settles in the best spot]

42
00:01:37,499 --> 00:01:40,699
[Sipping on morning coffee]

43
00:01:41,894 --> 00:01:42,699
This is so nice.

44
00:01:42,699 --> 00:01:43,494
[Taking in the pyramid view]

45
00:01:43,495 --> 00:01:44,899
Oh, but the view is insane.

46
00:01:45,084 --> 00:01:45,909
It feels like

47
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:49,617
[Feeling like ancient Egyptian royalty]
I'm Pharaoh's 6th cousin or something.

48
00:01:50,491 --> 00:01:52,988
[As he reveals his ambition to be a prince twice in a row]
I'm gonna be a prince today too.

49
00:01:52,989 --> 00:01:55,632
I promised myself all night long
as I was sleeping.

50
00:01:56,093 --> 00:01:56,984
Wow, bread.

51
00:01:56,984 --> 00:01:59,899
[YOHAN happily devours his breakfast]

52
00:02:00,732 --> 00:02:03,099
[Egyptian bread never lets you down]
Mhm! Mhm!! Mhm!!!

53
00:02:04,199 --> 00:02:05,666
[Crunchy]

54
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,798
[So happy with just a piece of bread]
This is really good.

55
00:02:09,999 --> 00:02:11,301
I'm actually
not a fan of those things.

56
00:02:11,302 --> 00:02:13,705
[Not a fan of American breakfast?]
I don't really like American breakfast.

57
00:02:14,532 --> 00:02:16,219
(The toast mukbang
of someone who doesn't like it)

58
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:16,917
Mhm!

59
00:02:18,329 --> 00:02:19,489
Why is it toasted perfectly?

60
00:02:19,490 --> 00:02:20,666
Mmm!

61
00:02:23,132 --> 00:02:26,432
[How much does he eat when he likes something then?]
Mhm!

62
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,699
[After getting full, he gets curious about the paupers]
They must get breakfast, right?

63
00:02:30,505 --> 00:02:32,598
[Technically, yes]
Agh…

64
00:02:35,066 --> 00:02:36,733
[One piece of bread]

65
00:02:37,199 --> 00:02:39,471
[And multivitamins]
Vitamins.

66
00:02:40,088 --> 00:02:41,005
This is kind of...

67
00:02:41,966 --> 00:02:43,166
[Utter disbelief]

68
00:02:44,879 --> 00:02:45,565
Look at this.

69
00:02:45,567 --> 00:02:47,099
You can't be a pauper again, huh?

70
00:02:47,306 --> 00:02:49,899
I'm totally gonna be a prince today.

71
00:02:51,266 --> 00:02:54,499
[The paupers eat their breakfast]

72
00:02:57,166 --> 00:02:59,899
[The mealtime is
filled with heavy silence]

73
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:01,709
[Even Romantic JOHNNY]
It's my first time eating

74
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:03,500
[struggles to eat plain bread in the morning]
bread that doesn't taste like anything.

75
00:03:03,638 --> 00:03:06,232
Is there a sauce
or anything to dip this in?

76
00:03:06,999 --> 00:03:08,498
[Miserable from the morning]
Ugh!!!

77
00:03:08,499 --> 00:03:10,199
It really doesn't
taste like anything.

78
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:14,099
[Meanwhile, the sandy wind shakes up their house]
I think we're gonna fly away, LEETEUK.

79
00:03:14,807 --> 00:03:16,991
Just looking at the condition
of our shoes from yesterday…

80
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:19,001
[In just one day,]
Hey, are we just paupers?

81
00:03:19,002 --> 00:03:21,699
[he got downgraded from NCT to pauper]
It's not that we look like paupers, we are paupers!

82
00:03:23,799 --> 00:03:25,799
How long do we have
to stay as paupers?

83
00:03:26,001 --> 00:03:27,599
[After tidying up and returning]
After you tidy up and return,

84
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,999
[Their status will be reset!]
your status will reset.

85
00:03:30,396 --> 00:03:31,670
Let's hurry up!

86
00:03:32,032 --> 00:03:34,299
[Let's escape this pauper life ASAP!]
Let's hurry up!

87
00:03:34,366 --> 00:03:37,466
(Quickly moving
to boost our status)

88
00:03:38,532 --> 00:03:41,199
[Escaping the dreadful tent]

89
00:03:41,592 --> 00:03:42,311
Let's go!

90
00:03:43,766 --> 00:03:46,699
[Next, JOHNNY]

91
00:03:46,699 --> 00:03:48,186
[and JISUNG escapes too!]

92
00:03:48,187 --> 00:03:50,299
Oh, JISUNG…

93
00:03:50,666 --> 00:03:53,366
[The prince fit they've been wearing since yesterday]
We were wearing the prince suits, right?

94
00:03:53,559 --> 00:03:56,159
So the suit was white at first,

95
00:03:56,399 --> 00:03:58,198
[Transformed into a Desert Sand edition]
but it's beige now.

96
00:03:58,199 --> 00:04:00,799
I just looked so pathetic.

97
00:04:00,999 --> 00:04:02,332
For me, being a pauper is…

98
00:04:02,566 --> 00:04:05,533
[Something he never wants to do again]
an experience where once is enough.

99
00:04:05,814 --> 00:04:06,466
Let's go.

100
00:04:06,466 --> 00:04:08,285
[There will be no more pauper life]

101
00:04:08,286 --> 00:04:09,166
Ugh, I'm feeling dizzy.

102
00:04:09,432 --> 00:04:10,532
[The first social status reset]

103
00:04:10,532 --> 00:04:14,798
Day 1 social status
resets in "ALL or NOTHING"!]

104
00:04:16,632 --> 00:04:18,914
[To get started
on their new itinerary]

105
00:04:18,915 --> 00:04:20,065
Alright, paupers, come on in!

106
00:04:20,066 --> 00:04:23,866
[WANGGEOZ are all gathered together again]
Oh, princes, you look great.

107
00:04:24,696 --> 00:04:25,798
Paupers, come on in.

108
00:04:25,799 --> 00:04:27,232
[They look worlds apart]
But your faces look refreshed.

109
00:04:27,566 --> 00:04:29,099
How was it, Team Pauper?

110
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,699
[Most interested in the pauper accommodation]
Seriously, how was it? Tell us exactly.

111
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:31,499
Since we have no idea.

112
00:04:31,699 --> 00:04:33,799
I'll be honest.
Look to the right side.

113
00:04:34,504 --> 00:04:36,732
[That's it right there]
It's that. Yeah, it's that.

114
00:04:37,223 --> 00:04:40,325
[Not the building in front]
You slept in a place that nice?

115
00:04:40,326 --> 00:04:43,098
[The mountains in the back]
You see that mountain at the end, right?

116
00:04:43,405 --> 00:04:44,799
- You see that mountain at the end, right?
- Oh, that mountain?

117
00:04:44,966 --> 00:04:46,211
Come on, don't lie.

118
00:04:46,212 --> 00:04:47,366
Come on,
it wouldn't be to that extent!

119
00:04:47,367 --> 00:04:49,500
It really doesn't seem like it, right?

120
00:04:49,501 --> 00:04:51,099
[It's so real that it's just funny...]
Just watch the broadcast.

121
00:04:51,432 --> 00:04:53,532
We slept in
a place like that, on the left.

122
00:04:53,999 --> 00:04:56,232
(Still doubtful)
No way, I don't believe you. I'll watch the show later.

123
00:04:56,699 --> 00:04:57,999
Did you all share a room?

124
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,299
[One tent!]
Yeah, just one tent.

125
00:04:59,599 --> 00:05:00,784
[A tent????]
Oh, it was a tent?

126
00:05:00,785 --> 00:05:02,296
Come on, don't lie.

127
00:05:02,297 --> 00:05:03,100
Come on!

128
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,832
[The princes just can't imagine it]
Who even uses tents these days?

129
00:05:04,833 --> 00:05:06,466
Yeah, why would
you use tents here?

130
00:05:06,466 --> 00:05:07,686
It's even funnier
that they don't believe us.

131
00:05:07,687 --> 00:05:09,466
[The communication struggle between classes]
This is why I'm being honest,

132
00:05:09,467 --> 00:05:10,566
because I didn't think
they'd believe me.

133
00:05:11,232 --> 00:05:12,499
You had a bed, right?

134
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:13,432
We did not.

135
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:15,099
[Your Highness… What tent has a bed?]
Come on!

136
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,206
It wasn't a bed,
but what was it called?

137
00:05:16,207 --> 00:05:17,100
[No beds, just sleeping bags]
A sleeping bag.

138
00:05:17,101 --> 00:05:17,666
A sleeping bag.

139
00:05:18,132 --> 00:05:19,065
Sleeping bags are nice!

140
00:05:19,065 --> 00:05:21,065
[Eyes shut tightly]

141
00:05:21,304 --> 00:05:23,211
- Sleeping bags are so warm.
- That must've been so romantic.

142
00:05:23,212 --> 00:05:25,404
[The silent pauper leader begins to stir]
But you can feel the rocks underneath. The gravel.

143
00:05:25,405 --> 00:05:25,966
Oh, come on.

144
00:05:26,419 --> 00:05:28,466
It's like a barren wasteland...

145
00:05:28,467 --> 00:05:30,099
No one would know
if a wolf came and snatched you away at night.

146
00:05:30,392 --> 00:05:33,025
I'd believe you
if you were bitten.

147
00:05:33,033 --> 00:05:35,432
I'd believe you if you were
bitten by a wolf, but you weren't.

148
00:05:35,766 --> 00:05:36,693
[Believe it or not]
You only drove on paved roads, huh?

149
00:05:36,694 --> 00:05:38,232
You only went
on smooth roads, huh?

150
00:05:38,966 --> 00:05:40,494
[Only the paupers find this funny]

151
00:05:40,495 --> 00:05:41,208
Why?

152
00:05:41,989 --> 00:05:43,391
We thought
our car was getting blasted.

153
00:05:43,392 --> 00:05:46,233
[Last night's exciting
off-road adventure]

154
00:05:46,399 --> 00:05:49,032
How much of
what we said do you believe?

155
00:05:49,566 --> 00:05:50,603
[Not a single word]
I believe none of it.

156
00:05:50,604 --> 00:05:51,805
Really?

157
00:05:51,805 --> 00:05:52,965
It's nonsense.

158
00:05:53,292 --> 00:05:54,932
[Instead of a blanket, the sand covered them]
You know, blankets? Do you know what it was?

159
00:05:54,933 --> 00:05:56,599
- What was the blanket?
- The blanket was sand.

160
00:05:57,099 --> 00:05:58,332
We were talking yesterday,

161
00:05:58,333 --> 00:05:59,999
and it felt like
sand was getting stuck in my teeth.

162
00:06:02,399 --> 00:06:04,591
You must've gotten
your teeth properly cleaned then.

163
00:06:04,592 --> 00:06:05,532
Definitely.

164
00:06:05,899 --> 00:06:06,889
It's kind of like this.

165
00:06:06,890 --> 00:06:08,218
(Subtly recommending it)
It's one of those experiences

166
00:06:08,219 --> 00:06:11,099
you should try
at least once in life.

167
00:06:11,498 --> 00:06:13,707
[Then you keep doing it]
You can keep experiencing it, then.

168
00:06:13,708 --> 00:06:14,699
Everyone, do you know this?

169
00:06:15,032 --> 00:06:16,599
The feeling of waking up,
opening your eyes,

170
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,699
and seeing
a pyramid in front of you?

171
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:19,999
- A pyramid?
- A pyramid was in front of you?

172
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,598
Seriously!

173
00:06:20,599 --> 00:06:22,032
[This time, a world the paupers can't even imagine]
That was the view when we woke up.

174
00:06:22,992 --> 00:06:24,410
- Amazing, right?
- It was a total pyramid view.

175
00:06:24,411 --> 00:06:25,497
[Just envious...]
And this is the terrace.

176
00:06:25,498 --> 00:06:26,710
You just open up
the terrace door…!

177
00:06:26,711 --> 00:06:27,799
Oh, it was really amazing!

178
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,832
The hotel was fantastic.

179
00:06:29,004 --> 00:06:30,389
[The paupers didn't even have time for photos…]
We had a mental breakdown yesterday,

180
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,896
so we didn't even think
to take pictures.

181
00:06:31,897 --> 00:06:33,299
Taking photos
didn't even cross our minds.

182
00:06:33,806 --> 00:06:35,706
After being a prince once…

183
00:06:35,707 --> 00:06:36,598
Was it so great?

184
00:06:36,599 --> 00:06:37,376
Wow…

185
00:06:37,377 --> 00:06:38,906
- I don't think I can go down from there.
- Yeah, I don't think I can.

186
00:06:38,907 --> 00:06:40,708
Yeah, DAWN,
your face looks better than yesterday.

187
00:06:40,709 --> 00:06:41,366
[Looking posh]
Yes.

188
00:06:41,592 --> 00:06:43,366
What worries me is that

189
00:06:43,367 --> 00:06:45,599
I feel like
I'll never become a prince.

190
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:48,500
I think LEETEUK still
doesn't understand yesterday's game.

191
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,899
[Still figuring out yesterday's game]

192
00:06:49,899 --> 00:06:50,899
Still?

193
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:51,899
Do it one more time.

194
00:06:53,232 --> 00:06:53,990
[About to take a break]
Take a break, everyone.

195
00:06:53,991 --> 00:06:55,465
- Oh, I'm so tired.
- I think we're almost there.

196
00:06:55,466 --> 00:06:56,832
[But they're already there?]
We're already there?

197
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,316
[It's an empty desert, where exactly is "almost there"?]
What do you mean we're there? There's nothing!

198
00:06:58,317 --> 00:06:59,582
No, this is the entrance
to the airport.

199
00:06:59,583 --> 00:07:00,166
Oh, really?

200
00:07:00,167 --> 00:07:01,688
SHINDONG,
this is where we slept.

201
00:07:01,689 --> 00:07:03,197
If someone told you
to sleep here, could you?

202
00:07:03,466 --> 00:07:05,297
[The clash between the princes and paupers continues]
They really don't believe us! It's getting annoying now.

203
00:07:05,298 --> 00:07:07,999
That's ridiculous.
Why would you sleep there?

204
00:07:07,999 --> 00:07:11,286
[Our second stop of the trip]
[Arrived at the actual destination!]

205
00:07:11,287 --> 00:07:12,107
We're almost at the airport.

206
00:07:12,108 --> 00:07:13,999
Let's go to our next stop!

207
00:07:14,418 --> 00:07:16,300
[The next stop is Luxor]
We'll see you at the next stop, Luxor!

208
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:17,465
Luxor?

209
00:07:17,605 --> 00:07:18,599
What's Luxor?

210
00:07:18,599 --> 00:07:21,665
[Heading to the second location
on a domestic flight]

211
00:07:23,266 --> 00:07:25,966
[On the east of the Nile River,
where the sun rises]

212
00:07:27,166 --> 00:07:29,471
[A land full of
brilliant ancient sites]

213
00:07:29,472 --> 00:07:32,099
[The land of the living]

214
00:07:33,159 --> 00:07:35,066
[The world’s greatest open-air museum]

215
00:07:35,766 --> 00:07:38,366
[And on the west of the Nile River,
where the sun sets]

216
00:07:39,025 --> 00:07:41,299
[The tombs of pharaohs]

217
00:07:42,332 --> 00:07:45,832
[and the temples
for royal burials stand tall]

218
00:07:47,732 --> 00:07:49,999
[The land of the dead]

219
00:07:54,358 --> 00:07:58,832
[A city where life and death coexist
on the east and west of the Nile]

220
00:08:00,699 --> 00:08:03,599
[LUXOR]

221
00:08:06,166 --> 00:08:09,498
[Arrived in Luxor, the second stop of the Egypt trip!]
Today's destination is Luxor.

222
00:08:09,499 --> 00:08:11,201
But it feels a bit quieter here.

223
00:08:11,202 --> 00:08:12,865
[Luxor's first impression is already perfect]
I think I like it more here.

224
00:08:12,866 --> 00:08:15,015
[A broader Nile River view than in Cairo]
The Nile River looks bigger here

225
00:08:15,015 --> 00:08:16,786
compared to
what we saw in Cairo.

226
00:08:16,786 --> 00:08:18,499
- It seems wider here.
- Yeah.

227
00:08:18,904 --> 00:08:20,132
And, like,

228
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:21,206
[So many horses on the street]
there are so many horses here.

229
00:08:21,207 --> 00:08:21,912
There really are so many horses.

230
00:08:21,913 --> 00:08:22,899
My guess is

231
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,912
[A horseback riding mission?]
we might end up riding horses

232
00:08:25,002 --> 00:08:26,499
I saw that thing at the Red Sea.

233
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,099
Riding horses along the Red Sea…

234
00:08:28,395 --> 00:08:31,292
[Saw in an Egypt-related video]
Where they run in the sea.

235
00:08:31,293 --> 00:08:32,499
An extreme sport.

236
00:08:32,686 --> 00:08:33,297
On horseback.

237
00:08:33,298 --> 00:08:34,113
[An activity they're hearing about for the first time]
In the water?

238
00:08:34,114 --> 00:08:36,099
- In the water?
- In the water, in the water.

239
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,366
- Really?
- Yes.

240
00:08:37,666 --> 00:08:39,932
[Let's have DAWN do that for sure]
I hope DAWN really rides a horse.

241
00:08:40,332 --> 00:08:41,832
[The second guess is an ancient site]
Is it an ancient site?

242
00:08:42,099 --> 00:08:43,832
[I like ancient sites]
Ancient sites sound fun.

243
00:08:44,299 --> 00:08:46,107
A treasure hunt
at an ancient site.

244
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:48,499
[Busy predicting the ancient site mission]
Maybe it's deciphering ancient languages?

245
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,103
Oh, we're already
at the ancient site!

246
00:08:50,104 --> 00:08:51,384
[The ancient sites come into
full view outside the window]

247
00:08:51,384 --> 00:08:52,733
Oh!

248
00:08:53,772 --> 00:08:55,096
[Truly feeling like a proper trip now]
It's really amazing!

249
00:08:55,097 --> 00:08:56,433
So, that's really huge.

250
00:08:57,514 --> 00:08:58,499
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

251
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,298
[The greatest open-air museum]
Wow! Look! Wow!

252
00:09:00,299 --> 00:09:01,694
It's a temple…
Why are there so many people?

253
00:09:01,695 --> 00:09:03,711
Wow!
Because it's a tourist spot.

254
00:09:03,712 --> 00:09:04,866
Wow, wow!

255
00:09:04,867 --> 00:09:07,566
[Totally captivated just looking out the window]
This place is really famous for its temples.

256
00:09:07,567 --> 00:09:09,791
Wow! How is this
still standing after all this time?

257
00:09:09,792 --> 00:09:10,799
This is so fascinating.

258
00:09:11,232 --> 00:09:12,899
There were
so many horses on the street.

259
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,666
And what was really impressive…

260
00:09:14,667 --> 00:09:16,333
Do I call it a temple?

261
00:09:16,334 --> 00:09:19,233
[History woven into everyday life]
Wow, it looked magnificent as it came into view.

262
00:09:19,402 --> 00:09:20,590
[Luxor is right up my alley]
"This place seems more my style."

263
00:09:20,591 --> 00:09:21,932
That thought crossed my mind.

264
00:09:22,632 --> 00:09:24,832
- So our team from yesterday is done now, right?
- Yes.

265
00:09:25,558 --> 00:09:27,899
But I hope
Team Pauper from yesterday

266
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,032
gets to sleep somewhere nice...

267
00:09:30,466 --> 00:09:31,787
[Ex-Team Pauper is touched]
He's so sweet!

268
00:09:31,788 --> 00:09:32,566
He's really sweet.

269
00:09:32,567 --> 00:09:34,027
…in a better pauper accommodation.

270
00:09:34,028 --> 00:09:35,308
Then, if that's the case…

271
00:09:36,799 --> 00:09:38,114
A comfortable
pauper accommodation?

272
00:09:38,115 --> 00:09:39,372
[Hoping for a pauper room upgrade]
Yes, a comfier pauper accommodation.

273
00:09:39,373 --> 00:09:40,866
Oh, yeah, that's nice.

274
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:43,999
[But the scenery starts to clear out]
There are many buildings, but not many people.

275
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:45,287
I feel like we're almost there.

276
00:09:45,288 --> 00:09:46,607
There's nothing here, though.
What is this?

277
00:09:46,608 --> 00:09:48,080
Oh, they're pulling the handbrake.

278
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:49,366
[Murmuring]
What's happening?

279
00:09:50,297 --> 00:09:51,398
They said we'd like it.

280
00:09:51,399 --> 00:09:54,806
[Just then,
the car leaves the road?!]

281
00:09:54,807 --> 00:09:57,065
[They enter a suspicious dirt road]
Oh, we're going off-road.

282
00:09:57,482 --> 00:09:59,409
We're almost at our destination.

283
00:09:59,410 --> 00:10:00,399
[The dirt path continues]

284
00:10:01,266 --> 00:10:02,690
[Anxiety creeps in]
I'm getting nervous again.

285
00:10:02,691 --> 00:10:05,512
But it suddenly feels like
we've entered the Amazon.

286
00:10:05,513 --> 00:10:07,512
This isn't gonna be
like surviving in the wilderness, right?

287
00:10:07,513 --> 00:10:08,765
[What exactly is today's mission…?]
Banana harvesting.

288
00:10:09,166 --> 00:10:10,199
It really felt…

289
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:12,665
like they were
taking us into the wild…

290
00:10:12,828 --> 00:10:15,990
[Is today's mission an extreme jungle adventure?!]
Is it like surviving on a deserted island?

291
00:10:15,991 --> 00:10:16,589
I thought
it was something like that.

292
00:10:16,590 --> 00:10:18,332
Like starting a fire from scratch.

293
00:10:19,706 --> 00:10:22,011
Oh? But all of a sudden…

294
00:10:22,232 --> 00:10:22,797
Are we getting on a boat?!

295
00:10:22,797 --> 00:10:23,665
What is it?

296
00:10:24,359 --> 00:10:27,459
[After passing
through a spooky banana field]

297
00:10:28,089 --> 00:10:29,103
Oh, what?

298
00:10:29,209 --> 00:10:31,233
Oh? We're getting on a boat!

299
00:10:31,317 --> 00:10:33,932
But I'm scared of boats.

300
00:10:34,399 --> 00:10:35,832
[Where exactly…]

301
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:38,299
[are we going…?]

302
00:10:39,032 --> 00:10:40,899
[Arrived at a mysterious spot]

303
00:10:43,366 --> 00:10:47,566
[Staff] One of the most
popular experiences in Egypt

304
00:10:47,567 --> 00:10:48,896
[The Nile River cruise tour]
is the Nile River cruise.

305
00:10:48,902 --> 00:10:50,539
Oh!

306
00:10:51,332 --> 00:10:54,132
[Everywhere you set foot
is an ancient site]

307
00:10:54,299 --> 00:10:58,299
[And the heart of Luxor,
the Nile River]

308
00:10:58,899 --> 00:11:01,066
[In a moving 5-star hotel]

309
00:11:01,599 --> 00:11:05,132
[Travel through
Luxor, the city of gods!]

310
00:11:05,499 --> 00:11:06,499
A cruiseee!!

311
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,966
We reserved

312
00:11:07,967 --> 00:11:10,689
[A 2-night, 3-day private cruise trip prepared]
2 nights and 3 days of luxury on a private cruise…

313
00:11:10,689 --> 00:11:11,815
- What?
- No way.

314
00:11:11,816 --> 00:11:13,366
…for all of you.

315
00:11:13,499 --> 00:11:15,099
Does the cruise set sail?
It doesn't, right?

316
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:16,083
[Of course, it sets sail]
It does.

317
00:11:16,084 --> 00:11:16,866
Really?

318
00:11:17,266 --> 00:11:20,733
I've never slept on a ship before.

319
00:11:21,199 --> 00:11:22,166
A cruise is insane!

320
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:23,699
What more needs to be said?

321
00:11:23,999 --> 00:11:24,988
[Getting off with high expectations]
Let's go.

322
00:11:24,989 --> 00:11:26,899
Wow, there are even rooms there!

323
00:11:27,005 --> 00:11:28,432
Oh!

324
00:11:28,433 --> 00:11:29,532
There's a pool!

325
00:11:29,676 --> 00:11:31,117
[There's a pool on this ship?!]
Wow!

326
00:11:31,118 --> 00:11:32,105
This place is amazing.

327
00:11:32,106 --> 00:11:32,878
Oh, what is this?

328
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,613
[Excitement explodes the moment they see it]
Isn’t this too good to be true?

329
00:11:34,614 --> 00:11:36,566
You should've told us
to bring swimsuits!

330
00:11:37,139 --> 00:11:40,199
[The grand cruise
awaits the WANGGEOZ]

331
00:11:40,766 --> 00:11:42,233
Isn't this too nice?

332
00:11:42,317 --> 00:11:43,704
Wow!

333
00:11:43,705 --> 00:11:44,684
Like, this is amazing!

334
00:11:44,685 --> 00:11:46,484
- Oh?
- Oh, wait, I'm nervous.

335
00:11:46,491 --> 00:11:47,492
Wow!

336
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:50,196
[Eyes wide open]
No, like…

337
00:11:50,596 --> 00:11:52,166
Wow!

338
00:11:52,167 --> 00:11:53,866
- This place is so luxurious!
- I know, right?

339
00:11:53,867 --> 00:11:54,596
Wow!

340
00:11:54,597 --> 00:11:56,065
[Revealing the ultimate luxury cruise]
Incredible!

341
00:11:56,599 --> 00:11:59,132
[Past the pool is…]

342
00:12:00,566 --> 00:12:02,533
[The lounge]

343
00:12:04,732 --> 00:12:07,865
[A cozy space
for the ultimate chill]

344
00:12:09,292 --> 00:12:13,359
[Beyond the private bar]

345
00:12:16,032 --> 00:12:18,632
[a dining room]

346
00:12:22,699 --> 00:12:24,132
What is this place?

347
00:12:24,133 --> 00:12:26,332
It's too fancy!

348
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:27,704
[Mesmerized by the luxury]
Wow, it's so luxurious.

349
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:29,932
- It smells amazing.
- Yeah, it smells so good.

350
00:12:29,933 --> 00:12:31,007
Open up that room.

351
00:12:31,008 --> 00:12:32,199
Wow, this is it! Wow!

352
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,799
- It's the suite, right?
- Yeah.

353
00:12:34,398 --> 00:12:36,265
Oh, wow!

354
00:12:36,266 --> 00:12:37,485
Wow, the game's over.

355
00:12:37,486 --> 00:12:39,732
- There's a TV.
- Wow, what is this place?

356
00:12:40,032 --> 00:12:42,765
[The main room
of the luxury cruise!]

357
00:12:43,932 --> 00:12:47,532
[A bed with a river view]

358
00:12:47,533 --> 00:12:49,933
[& a dining table]

359
00:12:50,366 --> 00:12:52,633
[Then step inside to find]

360
00:12:54,032 --> 00:12:57,799
[a comfy sofa
and a bathtub for relaxation]

361
00:12:59,199 --> 00:13:02,799
[A suite full of elegance]

362
00:13:04,672 --> 00:13:07,139
[And more premium rooms
with a similar layout!]

363
00:13:07,731 --> 00:13:08,812
Isn't this room
too good to be true?

364
00:13:08,813 --> 00:13:09,892
This room is
definitely the best one.

365
00:13:09,893 --> 00:13:11,580
[The more they explore, the more they want a cruise stay]
Yeah, this place…This place is…

366
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:12,797
This is the best room.

367
00:13:12,797 --> 00:13:14,590
Let's quickly get to the games
and just sleep.

368
00:13:14,591 --> 00:13:15,390
Sounds good.

369
00:13:15,391 --> 00:13:19,199
[Our cruise that left everyone mesmerized]
Let's sleep luxuriously tonight.

370
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,299
Oh, what now?

371
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,499
[Detecting something suspicious]
This setup feels weird.

372
00:13:22,499 --> 00:13:23,199
Oh, hold on.

373
00:13:23,416 --> 00:13:25,638
[Spotted the suitcases]
The luggage is here! The luggage is here!

374
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:27,699
[But the suitcases…]
What is this?

375
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,590
[are tied up?]
They're tied up! Wait.

376
00:13:29,591 --> 00:13:30,866
We have to crack the code?

377
00:13:31,932 --> 00:13:35,999
[Their suitcases are chained up]

378
00:13:37,132 --> 00:13:39,932
[You must unlock
the chains to take them]

379
00:13:39,933 --> 00:13:40,832
Oh, come on.

380
00:13:40,833 --> 00:13:43,232
(Assessing the situation)
Oh, so the mission is to get the codes…

381
00:13:43,233 --> 00:13:44,306
Aha!

382
00:13:44,307 --> 00:13:46,431
[It's a game with their suitcases on the line…]
This is going too far!

383
00:13:46,432 --> 00:13:47,791
[An even pettier start than expected]
Way too far!

384
00:13:47,792 --> 00:13:49,099
Oh, what is this?

385
00:13:49,305 --> 00:13:50,405
(It's not gonna be easy today either…)
If this is a 3-digit code…

386
00:13:50,406 --> 00:13:51,299
Hold on a second.

387
00:13:51,466 --> 00:13:52,866
This is legendary...

388
00:13:53,132 --> 00:13:54,499
There's a table here.

389
00:13:54,966 --> 00:13:56,900
[Looks suspicious to anyone]
There's a table here.

390
00:13:57,066 --> 00:13:59,233
It's an individual match.

391
00:13:59,532 --> 00:14:01,865
(Going solo today?)
So, the 1st place winner goes in

392
00:14:01,866 --> 00:14:03,591
[The winner gets first pick of the cruise cabins?]
and picks the room they want to use.

393
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:04,866
- They go in first?
- Yeah.

394
00:14:04,867 --> 00:14:05,682
Oh, it must be that.

395
00:14:05,683 --> 00:14:06,532
Is it?

396
00:14:06,533 --> 00:14:08,232
[This is making us dizzy]
What is it? Tell us!

397
00:14:08,466 --> 00:14:09,808
[Staff] As you've seen on the way,

398
00:14:09,809 --> 00:14:11,401
Your luggage

399
00:14:11,402 --> 00:14:13,798
[Locked with a 3-digit code]
is currently secured with a 3-digit lock.

400
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:14,697
It's locked.

401
00:14:14,698 --> 00:14:15,932
You must unlock

402
00:14:15,933 --> 00:14:17,399
[After unlocking the code,]
the 3-digit code,

403
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:19,065
[the first 3 people]
but only the first 3 people

404
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:21,399
[can hop on the cruise]
can board the luxury cruise.

405
00:14:21,466 --> 00:14:23,132
[A 4-event sports competition to become the princes of "The Solar Barque"]
[Today's main mission]

406
00:14:23,133 --> 00:14:26,399
[The Solar Barque]

407
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:30,532
[A sports competition with 4 events]

408
00:14:30,533 --> 00:14:32,006
[Reflexes / Dynamic vision]

409
00:14:32,007 --> 00:14:33,591
[Memory / Body fat burning]

410
00:14:33,592 --> 00:14:36,131
[The 4 events will be repeated]

411
00:14:36,325 --> 00:14:39,359
[Those who succeed or win]

412
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:41,399
[will acquire
one lock code at a time]

413
00:14:41,699 --> 00:14:45,831
[When there are 3 princes,
the game ends!]

414
00:14:46,799 --> 00:14:48,699
This is seriously legendary.

415
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,698
[Heh...]
This is crazy.

416
00:14:50,966 --> 00:14:52,565
[6 suitcases]
Are the numbers different for each suitcase?

417
00:14:52,566 --> 00:14:53,799
[Staff] Yes, they're all different.

418
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,202
[If you know 2 digits,]
But you just need to know 2 digits.

419
00:14:55,203 --> 00:14:57,066
[you can just guess the last digit]
Right, you can just narrow it down.

420
00:14:57,182 --> 00:14:59,191
[Anticipating that,]
Right, we thought you'd do that,

421
00:14:59,199 --> 00:15:00,699
[the suitcase numbers]
so the 3 numbers of the lock

422
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:01,899
[will be given at random]
will be given to you randomly!

423
00:15:01,899 --> 00:15:03,299
Agh!

424
00:15:03,632 --> 00:15:04,866
[Their sneaky plan fails]
You're too much.

425
00:15:04,867 --> 00:15:06,266
Ha…

426
00:15:06,266 --> 00:15:07,399
But…

427
00:15:07,399 --> 00:15:10,099
It's more annoying
that they predicted this.

428
00:15:10,566 --> 00:15:12,233
[Expecting a rough path ahead]
They're so smart, so smart.

429
00:15:12,234 --> 00:15:14,233
Then what about
the remaining 3 people?

430
00:15:14,233 --> 00:15:15,533
The other 3 people

431
00:15:15,534 --> 00:15:17,299
They'll probably sleep here.

432
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:19,299
[Legendary (negative)]
Wow, this is truly legendary.

433
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:22,798
[Not here]
We've rented an entire hotel for the staff.

434
00:15:22,799 --> 00:15:24,499
We'll lend you the rooftop.

435
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,999
[The place where today's paupers will sleep]
[The rooftop of the staff hotel!]

436
00:15:27,666 --> 00:15:29,399
The ship has many rooms…

437
00:15:29,559 --> 00:15:32,192
[Staff] We'll be filming,
so the staff needs to be on board, too.

438
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:32,819
Sorry about that.

439
00:15:32,819 --> 00:15:33,607
Oh…

440
00:15:33,607 --> 00:15:35,465
Then are we
doing this again tomorrow?

441
00:15:35,466 --> 00:15:37,099
[Pleading for sympathy]
I haven't…

442
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,266
properly unpacked yet.

443
00:15:39,666 --> 00:15:41,799
[Because there was no reason to unpack...]
Ugh…

444
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:44,066
Ugh…save me…

445
00:15:44,566 --> 00:15:45,591
[Thought we could sleep
comfortably tonight…]

446
00:15:45,591 --> 00:15:46,696
- Oh, yeah.
- Seriously.

447
00:15:46,697 --> 00:15:48,165
- That's true.
- Seriously.

448
00:15:48,424 --> 00:15:50,304
I can't remember
what's in my suitcase.

449
00:15:50,305 --> 00:15:51,531
[Troubled]
I can't remember.

450
00:15:52,806 --> 00:15:56,466
It's not gonna be easy
this time either.

451
00:15:56,467 --> 00:15:58,666
But that cruise suite room

452
00:15:58,667 --> 00:15:59,531
is mine.

453
00:16:00,599 --> 00:16:02,696
The cruise was
incredibly luxurious.

454
00:16:02,697 --> 00:16:03,966
It was spotless.

455
00:16:04,166 --> 00:16:06,098
[My bed is on the cruise!]
"This is where I'll sleep."

456
00:16:06,099 --> 00:16:07,233
That's what I thought.

457
00:16:07,399 --> 00:16:10,332
[Can't live as a pauper a second time]
No matter what happens, I must become a prince.

458
00:16:10,732 --> 00:16:12,332
[That's not happening!]
I was on the "Great Escape".

459
00:16:12,558 --> 00:16:14,373
[That prince title is mine]

460
00:16:14,374 --> 00:16:15,958
I'm Captain SHIN!

461
00:16:15,967 --> 00:16:16,994
[First game]
Then, we'll begin

462
00:16:16,995 --> 00:16:18,132
[Dynamic Vision Round]
the first event!

463
00:16:18,505 --> 00:16:19,800
[Using your dynamic vision,]
10.00.

464
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:20,599
[press the button at the 10-second mark]
Oh, we have to hit it then.

465
00:16:20,689 --> 00:16:23,465
- But it has to be 10.00?
- Yes.

466
00:16:23,466 --> 00:16:24,999
[Stop the timer]
There…Oh, exactly?

467
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,076
[at exactly 10 seconds to succeed]
You need to hit it exactly.

468
00:16:26,077 --> 00:16:28,599
The people who succeed
will get a number each.

469
00:16:29,032 --> 00:16:32,632
[Staff] Press the red button to start,
and the green button to reset.

470
00:16:32,966 --> 00:16:36,466
[Red = Start]
[Green = Reset]

471
00:16:36,467 --> 00:16:37,401
Here, like this and like this!

472
00:16:37,402 --> 00:16:38,394
Okay, okay! I got it.

473
00:16:39,432 --> 00:16:40,388
[Dynamic Vision]
DAWN.

474
00:16:40,389 --> 00:16:41,531
[DAWN's 10-second timer challenge]
This is…

475
00:16:41,532 --> 00:16:42,032
Ready!

476
00:16:42,466 --> 00:16:43,597
[For games like this]
Rhythm is key!

477
00:16:43,598 --> 00:16:44,599
Oh, that's right.

478
00:16:44,891 --> 00:16:46,165
I'll do it.

479
00:16:46,166 --> 00:16:46,991
Challenge accepted!

480
00:16:48,417 --> 00:16:49,212
1.

481
00:16:51,109 --> 00:16:51,910
1.

482
00:16:55,125 --> 00:16:57,566
[Rude]
[He's just finger-pointing]

483
00:16:57,567 --> 00:16:58,413
6.

484
00:16:59,778 --> 00:17:01,531
[Will the finger-pointing work?]
7. 8.

485
00:17:02,001 --> 00:17:02,632
9.

486
00:17:02,796 --> 00:17:03,531
10.

487
00:17:05,332 --> 00:17:07,299
[Did he succeed on the first try?]
Wow, wow, what?

488
00:17:07,419 --> 00:17:08,392
9.95 seconds.

489
00:17:09,499 --> 00:17:11,414
[Only 0.05 seconds off]
Okay, 9.95 seconds.

