[Is this really Egypt?]

2449
01:12:17,699 --> 01:12:19,476
But honestly, it was really great.

2450
01:12:19,477 --> 01:12:21,366
Seriously…
I usually dream…

2451
01:12:21,367 --> 01:12:22,678
I usually have
a hard time sleeping.

2452
01:12:22,678 --> 01:12:25,298
But last night,
I slept like a baby.

2453
01:12:25,299 --> 01:12:27,031
So, I felt great today.

2454
01:12:27,032 --> 01:12:29,199
As expected.

2455
01:12:29,200 --> 01:12:30,298
I think it'll be fun.

2456
01:12:30,299 --> 01:12:31,677
I've been thinking.

2457
01:12:31,678 --> 01:12:34,804
[What if one person is a pauper all the way?]
If one person were a pauper all the way,

2458
01:12:34,805 --> 01:12:35,866
that'd be so fun, too.

2459
01:12:35,867 --> 01:12:37,177
And you're our only hope.

2460
01:12:37,178 --> 01:12:38,265
That one person…

2461
01:12:38,266 --> 01:12:40,014
[The one and only pauper-all-the-way candidate]
So, you're our only shot.

2462
01:12:40,015 --> 01:12:40,932
Oh, it's just me.

2463
01:12:41,502 --> 01:12:45,065
This is fun.
I don't think I'll ever forget it.

2464
01:12:46,099 --> 01:12:48,599
But, being born and raised in Korea,

2465
01:12:49,959 --> 01:12:53,258
there's something I find interesting.

2466
01:12:53,271 --> 01:12:55,110
"What would it be like
to live in a country with one season?"

2467
01:12:55,118 --> 01:12:56,365
I imagine it a lot.

2468
01:12:56,366 --> 01:12:58,166
That is pretty fascinating.

2469
01:12:58,792 --> 01:13:04,398
For Egyptians…
Snow is one thing,

2470
01:13:04,399 --> 01:13:06,402
but they just don't
experience winter at all.

2471
01:13:06,403 --> 01:13:07,999
- I know, right?
- Right.

2472
01:13:08,366 --> 01:13:10,792
I bet it only rains
once or twice a year in Egypt...

2473
01:13:10,793 --> 01:13:11,866
Maybe once or twice.

2474
01:13:12,466 --> 01:13:14,590
[Cairo sees about 15 rainy days a year]
They have to try a steamed bun.

2475
01:13:14,591 --> 01:13:15,799
[Luxor hardly sees any rain]
They have to try a pizza steamed bun.

2476
01:13:15,799 --> 01:13:17,866
[However]

2477
01:13:18,832 --> 01:13:20,464
Is it raining?

2478
01:13:20,466 --> 01:13:21,398
Is it actually raining?

2479
01:13:21,399 --> 01:13:22,598
- Oh, it's raining!
- It's raining!

2480
01:13:22,598 --> 01:13:23,425
[It's suddenly raining…??]

2481
01:13:23,425 --> 01:13:25,366
We're sleeping outside, hold on…!

2482
01:13:26,932 --> 01:13:28,399
[Emergency...]
This is an emergency.

2483
01:13:28,787 --> 01:13:29,899
Hey, we're in trouble.

2484
01:13:29,900 --> 01:13:33,599
[What are the odds of seeing rain in Luxor…?]
Of all days, it just had to be today.

2485
01:13:33,965 --> 01:13:35,913
On top of that,
we have to pitch the tent ourselves.

2486
01:13:35,914 --> 01:13:37,199
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

2487
01:13:37,499 --> 01:13:39,790
While getting
soaked in the rain...

2488
01:13:39,791 --> 01:13:41,507
[Suddenly camping in the rain]
Wait, this is a bit…

2489
01:13:41,508 --> 01:13:43,296
They said it's a nice place.

2490
01:13:43,297 --> 01:13:44,677
Hold on a second!

2491
01:13:45,166 --> 01:13:47,499
[Feeling strangely uneasy...]
This is kind of weird.

2492
01:13:47,500 --> 01:13:51,092
Then, when we arrive,
will bread be waiting for us as our dinner?

2493
01:13:51,092 --> 01:13:53,799
[When it rains,
it pours for these paupers]

2494
01:13:55,166 --> 01:13:57,199
[After driving for a while,]

2495
01:13:57,200 --> 01:13:58,004
[an eerie scene unfolds]

2496
01:13:58,005 --> 01:13:59,314
Wait a second.

2497
01:13:59,315 --> 01:14:00,698
Are we…

2498
01:14:00,699 --> 01:14:01,514
What is this place?

2499
01:14:01,515 --> 01:14:02,331
Hold on, why this way…?

2500
01:14:02,332 --> 01:14:03,177
It feels like
a ghost will pop out…

2501
01:14:03,178 --> 01:14:04,631
What is this?

2502
01:14:04,632 --> 01:14:07,299
Did we take a wrong turn?
No way...

2503
01:14:07,495 --> 01:14:10,332
[With the tension rising]
Please, please, please.

2504
01:14:10,932 --> 01:14:13,832
[Where are the paupers headed?]

2505
01:14:13,832 --> 01:14:15,298
[The life of a prince]

2506
01:14:15,299 --> 01:14:17,698
LEETEUK!

2507
01:14:17,699 --> 01:14:18,677
LEETEUK!

2508
01:14:19,099 --> 01:14:23,165
JOHNNY, I just looked,

2509
01:14:23,166 --> 01:14:24,566
and the boat's moving.

2510
01:14:24,776 --> 01:14:26,677
I was looking outside.

2511
01:14:26,678 --> 01:14:28,810
The boat is moving, right?

2512
01:14:28,811 --> 01:14:29,918
Huh?

2513
01:14:29,919 --> 01:14:31,631
But I don't feel a thing...

2514
01:14:31,632 --> 01:14:32,177
Hold on.

2515
01:14:32,178 --> 01:14:33,375
Why?

2516
01:14:33,376 --> 01:14:34,799
I feel nothing at all.

2517
01:14:34,800 --> 01:14:36,401
No, I'm dizzy,
I'm feeling dizzy right now.

2518
01:14:36,402 --> 01:14:37,099
Really?

2519
01:14:37,100 --> 01:14:38,391
I'm really sensitive.

2520
01:14:38,392 --> 01:14:39,402
Wow, you're really sensitive.

2521
01:14:39,403 --> 01:14:40,177
Yeah.

2522
01:14:41,432 --> 01:14:43,303
[The princes' cruise sets sail]
We're moving, we're moving!

2523
01:14:43,304 --> 01:14:44,232
It's moving!
Wow, amazing!

2524
01:14:45,299 --> 01:14:49,099
[An exclusive service,
just for the princes]

2525
01:14:49,932 --> 01:14:55,299
[Enjoying Luxor on the water]

2526
01:14:56,932 --> 01:15:00,332
[And inside, the princes find ease]
Wow, there's even wifi too. This is awesome.

2527
01:15:01,566 --> 01:15:02,178
One Coke.

2528
01:15:02,178 --> 01:15:03,281
- One Coke?
- Yes.

2529
01:15:04,706 --> 01:15:06,600
[Instantly served]
Ice?

2530
01:15:06,601 --> 01:15:08,899
Yes, ice, ice!

2531
01:15:09,399 --> 01:15:10,405
Do you have beer?

2532
01:15:10,406 --> 01:15:11,018
One beer?

2533
01:15:11,019 --> 01:15:11,692
One beer, please.

2534
01:15:11,693 --> 01:15:13,166
- Oh, two beers!
- Oh, two beers!

2535
01:15:13,499 --> 01:15:14,713
[Ask and you shall receive
on the cruise]

2536
01:15:14,714 --> 01:15:16,365
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

2537
01:15:16,366 --> 01:15:19,447
It's the first time
I've seen ice here.

2538
01:15:19,494 --> 01:15:21,089
[Precious ice]
It's my first time seeing ice.

2539
01:15:21,090 --> 01:15:21,904
This is really valuable right now.

2540
01:15:21,904 --> 01:15:23,178
That's right.

2541
01:15:23,532 --> 01:15:26,999
Princes!

2542
01:15:27,399 --> 01:15:29,910
Here's looking at you, kid!

2543
01:15:29,911 --> 01:15:31,666
Oh my God.

2544
01:15:34,999 --> 01:15:36,910
[This is the taste of success]
Wow!

2545
01:15:36,911 --> 01:15:38,309
It's great to sip something cold.

2546
01:15:38,310 --> 01:15:39,399
So nice.

2547
01:15:40,799 --> 01:15:43,198
I can't help but smile.

2548
01:15:43,199 --> 01:15:44,166
You feel so happy, huh?

2549
01:15:44,166 --> 01:15:44,798
I feel so happy.

2550
01:15:44,799 --> 01:15:45,606
Was it like this yesterday?

2551
01:15:45,607 --> 01:15:47,084
Oh, it was like this yesterday.

2552
01:15:47,085 --> 01:15:48,799
[This lighting]
But today,

2553
01:15:48,800 --> 01:15:50,290
[This temperature]
we can enjoy it even more.

2554
01:15:50,291 --> 01:15:51,566
Exactly.

2555
01:15:51,566 --> 01:15:52,604
[This humidity…Perfect]

2556
01:15:52,604 --> 01:15:55,199
- Princes! Princes!
- Princes!

2557
01:15:55,778 --> 01:15:58,332
[This is what being a prince is all about]
Wow, this place is nice.

2558
01:15:58,932 --> 01:16:00,299
My name is Princess.

2559
01:16:00,300 --> 01:16:01,500
Oops.

2560
01:16:01,699 --> 01:16:04,699
[Oh, you're a princess?]
Princess?

2561
01:16:05,033 --> 01:16:06,511
[Oops...]
Oh, sorry.

2562
01:16:06,512 --> 01:16:07,998
My name is Prince.

2563
01:16:07,999 --> 01:16:09,288
[Prince = Amir]
Prince Amir.

2564
01:16:09,289 --> 01:16:10,677
- Amir.
- Amir, yep.

2565
01:16:10,678 --> 01:16:11,766
Prince Amir.

2566
01:16:12,007 --> 01:16:13,599
(Prince 1)
Amir 1.

2567
01:16:13,600 --> 01:16:14,704
(Prince 2)
Amir 2.

2568
01:16:14,705 --> 01:16:16,366
[Former princess (Prince 3)]
Amir 3, yeah.

2569
01:16:16,532 --> 01:16:17,998
Thank you!

2570
01:16:17,999 --> 01:16:19,677
Peace be upon you!

2571
01:16:19,678 --> 01:16:20,477
Oh!

2572
01:16:20,478 --> 01:16:21,677
[Oh yeah!]
LEETEUK, you're amazing.

2573
01:16:21,678 --> 01:16:22,677
Oh!

2574
01:16:23,332 --> 01:16:25,398
What's for dinner?

2575
01:16:25,866 --> 01:16:27,899
[The blessing time never ends]
Steak, pasta.

2576
01:16:27,999 --> 01:16:30,032
M-m-mushroom soup.

2577
01:16:30,238 --> 01:16:32,771
Okay, I'll speak with the chef.

2578
01:16:32,999 --> 01:16:34,584
[There's a chef…???]
Oh, he said he'll tell the chef.

2579
01:16:34,585 --> 01:16:35,899
Wow!

2580
01:16:35,899 --> 01:16:38,132
This feels awkward for me.

2581
01:16:38,140 --> 01:16:39,806
It's awkward to
order something and have it come out.

2582
01:16:39,807 --> 01:16:41,709
[At your service]
It's usually not like this, but the chef is doing it!

2583
01:16:41,710 --> 01:16:44,499
[A customized dining experience just for the princes]
Hey, then let's just order everything.

2584
01:16:44,678 --> 01:16:46,100
Kimchi…Kimchi stew?

2585
01:16:46,101 --> 01:16:48,203
Pizza?

2586
01:16:48,205 --> 01:16:49,899
[Okay, order received]
Do you have Margherita?

2587
01:16:49,900 --> 01:16:51,132
Yeah, Margherita. Yeah.

2588
01:16:51,133 --> 01:16:53,176
[Even ordered steak, while they're at it]
We want medium.

2589
01:16:53,177 --> 01:16:54,796
- No, no.
- I want well done.

2590
01:16:54,797 --> 01:16:55,999
No, no.

2591
01:16:56,000 --> 01:16:58,266
Medium well done.

2592
01:16:58,699 --> 01:17:00,031
Medium.

2593
01:17:00,032 --> 01:17:01,465
Well done.

2594
01:17:01,466 --> 01:17:03,366
Medium well.

2595
01:17:03,766 --> 01:17:06,765
[They each have different steak preferences]
Yes, yes.

2596
01:17:06,766 --> 01:17:09,304
[Unlike their demanding taste buds,]
You know, you know, check, check.

2597
01:17:09,305 --> 01:17:09,997
Steak check.

2598
01:17:09,997 --> 01:17:13,633
[they're unable to hide their past pauper vibes]
Oh, why am I embarrassed?

2599
01:17:14,005 --> 01:17:15,783
My socks are a pauper's.

2600
01:17:15,784 --> 01:17:16,632
Hey, my socks...

2601
01:17:17,206 --> 01:17:19,306
- My socks are a pauper's.
- Me too.

2602
01:17:19,307 --> 01:17:20,565
[The hard-earned upgrade to royalty]
Hey, you're a pauper too.

2603
01:17:21,132 --> 01:17:24,765
[It's a night full of laughter]

2604
01:17:26,332 --> 01:17:28,898
I feel more grateful
for the little things.

2605
01:17:28,899 --> 01:17:31,314
Cold water...

2606
01:17:31,315 --> 01:17:32,466
Ice...

2607
01:17:32,974 --> 01:17:36,275
[The prince's newfound peace of mind]
The food that appears when you order.

2608
01:17:36,276 --> 01:17:39,199
I realized how
precious these things were.

2609
01:17:40,099 --> 01:17:42,866
[The laughter never ends in a prince's life]
I'm so happy I can't stop laughing!

2610
01:17:42,866 --> 01:17:45,966
[The pauper's life]
[Meanwhile...]

2611
01:17:47,132 --> 01:17:48,006
[Paupers arrive at an unknown location]
What, is it here?

2612
01:17:48,007 --> 01:17:49,006
Hold on, why this way…?

2613
01:17:49,007 --> 01:17:50,599
- It feels like a ghost will pop out…
- What is this?

2614
01:17:50,600 --> 01:17:51,487
(Where are we?)
Did we take a wrong turn?

2615
01:17:51,488 --> 01:17:53,599
Oh, we must have
taken a wrong turn, right?

2616
01:17:54,191 --> 01:17:55,785
[Suspicious, but getting out of the car]
Oh, what's this?

2617
01:17:55,786 --> 01:17:57,599
This is the place?

2618
01:17:59,194 --> 01:18:01,632
Wow, what's this?

2619
01:18:01,633 --> 01:18:02,998
Isn't this pretty decent?

2620
01:18:02,999 --> 01:18:04,999
Wait, are we
setting up a tent here?

2621
01:18:05,201 --> 01:18:05,865
Oh, the rooftop.

2622
01:18:05,866 --> 01:18:07,677
This is the rooftop?

2623
01:18:08,564 --> 01:18:11,604
[Today's pauper accommodation]

2624
01:18:12,125 --> 01:18:15,065
[The staff accommodation]

2625
01:18:15,066 --> 01:18:17,899
[The rooftop
of the staff accommodation]

2626
01:18:19,566 --> 01:18:20,678
[No elevators]

2627
01:18:20,678 --> 01:18:23,794
[The stairs will
take you to the rooftop]

2628
01:18:23,796 --> 01:18:24,533
Whoa, this is insane.

2629
01:18:25,632 --> 01:18:28,499
Hold on, this is so tiring!

2630
01:18:29,132 --> 01:18:32,308
Where are we? Is this it?

2631
01:18:32,309 --> 01:18:33,494
Huh?

2632
01:18:33,901 --> 01:18:35,016
- If it's this…!
- Wow, the breeze is nice

2633
01:18:35,017 --> 01:18:36,389
- What?!
- This is nice!

2634
01:18:36,389 --> 01:18:37,398
What's this?

2635
01:18:37,399 --> 01:18:39,194
- This is so pleasant.
- It's so nice.

2636
01:18:39,195 --> 01:18:41,298
- This is pretty decent.
- I'm happy with it.

2637
01:18:41,299 --> 01:18:42,299
- Oh!
- JISUNG, what do you think? Is this okay?

2638
01:18:42,300 --> 01:18:43,616
[Way better than expected!]
Crazy! It's crazy!

2639
01:18:43,617 --> 01:18:44,296
This is nice.

2640
01:18:44,297 --> 01:18:44,911
This is what
being a king is about!

2641
01:18:44,912 --> 01:18:46,366
Hey, hey, look at that!

2642
01:18:46,504 --> 01:18:47,166
Wow!

2643
01:18:47,167 --> 01:18:48,505
[The pauper accommodation they can't stop raving about?]
Wow!

2644
01:18:48,506 --> 01:18:50,266
Wow, look at this view! Just wow!

2645
01:18:50,267 --> 01:18:51,020
This is seriously amazing!

2646
01:18:51,021 --> 01:18:51,899
This place has an amazing view!

2647
01:18:51,900 --> 01:18:53,104
Wow, I'm so impressed.
This place is insane.

2648
01:18:53,105 --> 01:18:54,400
[A smooth rooftop floor]

2649
01:18:54,899 --> 01:18:58,632
[A breathtaking view
of the ancient sites in the back]

2650
01:18:59,432 --> 01:19:02,432
[The Valley of the Kings]

2651
01:19:02,999 --> 01:19:05,932
[The pharaoh's secret tomb,
which was hidden deep inside a rocky mountain]

2652
01:19:06,632 --> 01:19:11,099
[to escape the endless
tomb raiding of the pyramids]

2653
01:19:12,999 --> 01:19:15,899
[Serving as a royal burial ground for pharaohs
from the 16th to the 11th century BC,]

2654
01:19:15,900 --> 01:19:19,232
[it provides a glimpse into the religion,
art, and funeral customs of the time]

2655
01:19:20,832 --> 01:19:24,731
[The final resting place
where pharaohs dreamed of eternity]

2656
01:19:25,632 --> 01:19:29,065
[And that very place
stretches out behind them]

2657
01:19:30,999 --> 01:19:33,165
This is amazing!
The view is fantastic.

2658
01:19:33,166 --> 01:19:34,806
The scenery is so beautiful.

2659
01:19:34,806 --> 01:19:35,799
Isn't this a painting?

2660
01:19:35,799 --> 01:19:37,192
- It's so gorgeous.
- I know, right?

2661
01:19:37,193 --> 01:19:39,100
Wow, the breeze is so refreshing.

2662
01:19:39,101 --> 01:19:40,532
The weather's just perfect right now.

2663
01:19:40,876 --> 01:19:42,585
[The 2nd generation paupers are satisfied]
Wow, this is more than enough.

2664
01:19:42,586 --> 01:19:43,499
I'm completely satisfied.

2665
01:19:43,500 --> 01:19:45,599
- We're basically princes at this point.
- We're really princes.

2666
01:19:45,600 --> 01:19:48,232
[Awesome]
This is something worth experiencing at least once.

2667
01:19:48,671 --> 01:19:51,958
[A minimal pauper kit]
They give us exactly 3 bottles of water.

2668
01:19:52,525 --> 01:19:54,082
And heat packs.

2669
01:19:54,090 --> 01:19:56,231
- Is that food?
- It's a humidifying mask.

2670
01:19:56,866 --> 01:19:58,599
[The paupert shares his knowledge with the rookie paupers]
I'm a pauper expert.

2671
01:19:58,600 --> 01:19:59,678
I'm a paupert.

2672
01:19:59,678 --> 01:20:00,399
This is our food?

2673
01:20:00,400 --> 01:20:01,528
Yeah, we did
have it for breakfast.

2674
01:20:01,529 --> 01:20:02,499
Oh, really?

2675
01:20:02,999 --> 01:20:04,590
But the floor here is pretty good.

2676
01:20:04,591 --> 01:20:06,091
- Isn't this pretty decent?
- It's amazing.

2677
01:20:06,092 --> 01:20:07,813
[Can immediately go to bed]
I could just fall asleep right here.

2678
01:20:07,814 --> 01:20:08,776
This is really nice.

2679
01:20:08,776 --> 01:20:11,677
[The paupert's body moves on instinct]
JISUNG knows how to do it. Do we just open it up?

2680
01:20:11,677 --> 01:20:13,677
You just have to open it up.

2681
01:20:13,678 --> 01:20:14,615
Right here.

2682
01:20:14,616 --> 01:20:16,201
- Like this, like this.
- That's right.

2683
01:20:16,202 --> 01:20:17,820
[Under the paupert's management, the tent setup begins]
Oh, okay, okay.

2684
01:20:17,821 --> 01:20:18,678
Oh, here's the strap.

2685
01:20:18,678 --> 01:20:20,499
We can hang it on this strap.

2686
01:20:20,988 --> 01:20:22,496
Oh, this is good.
It's more than enough.

2687
01:20:22,505 --> 01:20:24,677
- Not too bad!
- It's nice!

2688
01:20:25,166 --> 01:20:26,678
But if you go inside…

2689
01:20:26,999 --> 01:20:27,677
Did it get bigger…?

2690
01:20:27,678 --> 01:20:28,766
Oh, it's spacious!

2691
01:20:29,299 --> 01:20:30,785
[It feels like it got bigger overnight]
But why does it suddenly feel more spacious?

2692
01:20:30,786 --> 01:20:32,932
Hey, three people
can easily sleep here.

2693
01:20:33,266 --> 01:20:34,678
Was the tent always this big?

2694
01:20:34,678 --> 01:20:35,677
There's another one of these.

2695
01:20:36,132 --> 01:20:37,731
- Was it always this size?
- There's another one?

2696
01:20:37,732 --> 01:20:39,032
Was it always like this?

2697
01:20:39,532 --> 01:20:41,398
[Yes, it's the same tent]
I don't believe it.

2698
01:20:41,399 --> 01:20:42,908
JISUNG, just where
did you go last night?

2699
01:20:42,909 --> 01:20:44,299
I have no idea.

2700
01:20:44,499 --> 01:20:45,912
Just how did you guys
sleep last night?

2701
01:20:45,913 --> 01:20:48,331
Why'd you keep saying
it wasn't good when it's so nice?

2702
01:20:48,332 --> 01:20:49,578
You lied, huh???

2703
01:20:49,579 --> 01:20:50,395
Seriously!

2704
01:20:50,396 --> 01:20:51,495
Why would you say it like that?

2705
01:20:51,496 --> 01:20:53,765
Hey, this is so nice.

2706
01:20:53,766 --> 01:20:57,100
[Was it all a mirage yesterday?]
Was I too negative…?

2707
01:20:58,766 --> 01:21:00,399
No, but I'm sure…

2708
01:21:00,400 --> 01:21:03,399
(Squeezed in)
I slept so close to JOHNNY.

2709
01:21:03,932 --> 01:21:04,992
[Confused]

2710
01:21:04,993 --> 01:21:06,899
Wow, what is this?

2711
01:21:07,225 --> 01:21:08,768
JISUNG, this is so nice!

2712
01:21:08,776 --> 01:21:09,799
Oh, but…

2713
01:21:09,800 --> 01:21:11,799
[Still skeptical]
Is this really the same tent?

2714
01:21:12,566 --> 01:21:15,666
[Get it together and help with the sleeping bag]
Can you pull this out?

2715
01:21:16,332 --> 01:21:19,965
[No clue what's going on...]

2716
01:21:21,005 --> 01:21:25,105
[Today's aesthetic accommodation
that only JISUNG is confused by]

2717
01:21:25,599 --> 01:21:26,696
[So nice]

2718
01:21:26,697 --> 01:21:27,677
And then now…

2719
01:21:28,388 --> 01:21:30,389
- Hey, hey!
- Oh, what's this?

2720
01:21:30,390 --> 01:21:32,292
And then now…

2721
01:21:32,293 --> 01:21:33,427
- Hey, hey!
- Oh, what's this?

2722
01:21:33,428 --> 01:21:34,703
[With the paupert's lead, the club opens]
Hey, let's play some music!

2723
01:21:34,704 --> 01:21:36,232
Oh, this is nice!

2724
01:21:36,678 --> 01:21:38,987
[Just go with the beat]

2725
01:21:38,987 --> 01:21:41,098
- Oho!
- Ppa ppa-ppa ppa-ppa-ppa!

2726
01:21:41,099 --> 01:21:42,898
Egyptian Nights!

2727
01:21:42,899 --> 01:21:44,608
Arabian Nights!

2728
01:21:44,609 --> 01:21:46,011
It's Arabian Nights!

2729
01:21:46,012 --> 01:21:46,579
Oh, I'm dizzy.

2730
01:21:46,580 --> 01:21:49,339
[The paupers have a blast
with just a light]

2731
01:21:49,493 --> 01:21:50,566
Oh, tomorrow…

2732
01:21:50,567 --> 01:21:52,331
I feel kind of bad for the princes.

2733
01:21:52,332 --> 01:21:54,098
Let's pretend
we had it rough tomorrow.

2734
01:21:54,099 --> 01:21:56,175
[Planning to look as miserable as possible]
Yeah, we gotta act like we struggled.

2735
01:21:56,176 --> 01:21:56,975
For sure.

2736
01:21:56,976 --> 01:21:58,380
If they find out
we slept comfortably like this…

2737
01:21:58,380 --> 01:21:59,598
Totally.

2738
01:21:59,599 --> 01:22:02,199
LEETEUK will
start grumbling again. You know?

2739
01:22:02,199 --> 01:22:03,332
Ugh!!!

2740
01:22:04,432 --> 01:22:06,098
Was yesterday romantic?
Or is today romantic?

2741
01:22:06,099 --> 01:22:07,305
Today is romantic.

2742
01:22:07,306 --> 01:22:09,802
Did you know you can
see the stars? Look up!

2743
01:22:09,803 --> 01:22:10,510
You can see the stars.

2744
01:22:10,511 --> 01:22:12,109
I saw the stars earlier.

2745
01:22:12,110 --> 01:22:12,795
You can see the stars.

2746
01:22:12,796 --> 01:22:15,630
[The romantic paupers have the luxury to look up at the sky]
Once the lights are out, they'll be really visible.

2747
01:22:16,203 --> 01:22:18,209
Oh, hold on!
This is so nice!

2748
01:22:18,210 --> 01:22:19,495
[Not a single thing to complain about]
Wow!

2749
01:22:19,496 --> 01:22:20,887
- Wow, unbelievable.
- I think I can sleep here.

2750
01:22:20,888 --> 01:22:22,332
This is insane.

2751
01:22:22,966 --> 01:22:25,989
There was nothing different
from the pyramids that I saw at the hotel.

2752
01:22:25,990 --> 01:22:27,398
It was so breathtaking.

2753
01:22:27,399 --> 01:22:28,976
And there was a nice breeze.

2754
01:22:28,977 --> 01:22:29,666
Gasp!

2755
01:22:30,566 --> 01:22:33,198
I really loved it.
It just felt like a camping trip.

2756
01:22:33,713 --> 01:22:36,831
I could fall asleep right now.

2757
01:22:36,832 --> 01:22:38,365
I might just pass out.

2758
01:22:38,626 --> 01:22:40,626
[Sleepy]

2759
01:22:42,703 --> 01:22:44,786
[A spot too good to give up]
[And the princes who don't want to fall asleep]

2760
01:22:44,786 --> 01:22:46,499
- Steak.
- Wow!

2761
01:22:47,132 --> 01:22:49,014
They must really be
making it in the kitchen downstairs.

2762
01:22:49,015 --> 01:22:50,777
- Medium well done.
- Medium well.

2763
01:22:50,778 --> 01:22:51,899
Yes!

2764
01:22:53,058 --> 01:22:54,057
Oh, pizza, pizza!

2765
01:22:54,058 --> 01:22:56,332
[The glorious food comes one after the other]
Oh! Oh! Oh!

2766
01:22:56,999 --> 01:22:58,024
[Steak cooked to everyone's liking]
Wow!

2767
01:22:58,025 --> 01:22:59,899
This looks seriously delicious.

2768
01:23:00,132 --> 01:23:02,499
[The soup Prince Amir LEETEUK ordered]
Mushroom! Wow!

2769
01:23:02,905 --> 01:23:05,099
- Wow!
- LEETEUK, you really ordered well.

2770
01:23:05,100 --> 01:23:06,566
[A dining experience, exclusive to the princes]
Right? Right?

2771
01:23:07,232 --> 01:23:09,665
[The prince's elegant knife action]

2772
01:23:10,496 --> 01:23:11,694
How is it?

2773
01:23:11,695 --> 01:23:12,614
Is it tasty?

2774
01:23:12,622 --> 01:23:13,766
Mmm!

2775
01:23:18,199 --> 01:23:19,295
Mmm, delicious!

2776
01:23:19,301 --> 01:23:20,365
It tastes great!

2777
01:23:20,878 --> 01:23:23,057
Salmon and cream cheese.

2778
01:23:23,504 --> 01:23:25,078
Mmm!

2779
01:23:25,712 --> 01:23:26,999
[Salmon + avocado]
Oh, it's smoked.

2780
01:23:27,000 --> 01:23:28,232
[Maximizing the light and mild flavors]
It's delicious.

2781
01:23:29,966 --> 01:23:32,333
It's the taste of success.

2782
01:23:32,732 --> 01:23:33,887
I want to
sleep here again tomorrow.

2783
01:23:33,888 --> 01:23:35,184
Me too.

2784
01:23:35,185 --> 01:23:36,699
I know, right?

2785
01:23:37,132 --> 01:23:40,099
Honestly, I want to be
the prince a few more times.

2786
01:23:40,366 --> 01:23:42,613
[Why are you stating the obvious?]
I think everyone feels the same.

2787
01:23:42,932 --> 01:23:43,707
I wonder what we're doing tomorrow.

2788
01:23:43,708 --> 01:23:45,817
Since we did
individual matches today…

2789
01:23:46,166 --> 01:23:47,383
[The princes get ready for tomorrow]
It'll probably be 6 vs 6 tomorrow.

2790
01:23:47,384 --> 01:23:48,618
Oh!

2791
01:23:48,810 --> 01:23:49,965
I feel like
it'll be something like that.

2792
01:23:49,966 --> 01:23:51,466
I think it'll be
something huge tomorrow!

2793
01:23:51,683 --> 01:23:52,865
Because…

2794
01:23:52,871 --> 01:23:55,190
Today, we started late

2795
01:23:55,191 --> 01:23:56,598
because we had to travel.

2796
01:23:57,366 --> 01:23:59,133
Tomorrow,
we'll be here all day.

2797
01:24:00,599 --> 01:24:02,999
From what I can tell,
they're gonna use

2798
01:24:03,379 --> 01:24:04,894
whatever they can in this area

2799
01:24:04,895 --> 01:24:06,413
- and play games.
- Right, right.

2800
01:24:06,414 --> 01:24:07,699
I think it'll involve
the ancient sites.

2801
01:24:08,107 --> 01:24:09,902
Then tomorrow, we'll definitely
do horseback riding or an activity.

2802
01:24:09,903 --> 01:24:10,904
It'll definitely be
one of the two.

2803
01:24:10,905 --> 01:24:11,999
Yeah, I think
we'll definitely do it.

2804
01:24:12,000 --> 01:24:13,399
For sure,
it's one of those two, right?

2805
01:24:13,399 --> 01:24:14,932
[What kind of game will it be?]

2806
01:24:15,166 --> 01:24:18,890
[On the next episode]
A life-changing opportunity is waiting for you.

2807
01:24:19,164 --> 01:24:20,017
What could that be?

2808
01:24:20,174 --> 01:24:20,993
Whoa, what's this place?

2809
01:24:20,994 --> 01:24:22,237
[Taking place at the Luxor market]
The deeper we go, the cooler it gets.

2810
01:24:22,238 --> 01:24:24,108
Wow, I just saw
something amazing.

2811
01:24:24,109 --> 01:24:25,313
[The paupers' hidden mission]
A treasure hunt or something.

2812
01:24:25,313 --> 01:24:26,331
A treasure hunt?

2813
01:24:26,332 --> 01:24:27,707
This is hard, so hard.

2814
01:24:27,708 --> 01:24:29,019
How are we supposed to do this?

2815
01:24:29,020 --> 01:24:30,475
[The one dreaming of a status upgrade]
How do I do this?

2816
01:24:30,476 --> 01:24:31,798
I can't help!

2817
01:24:31,799 --> 01:24:33,631
[Why...]
I'm not happy.

2818
01:24:33,632 --> 01:24:34,795
[Overcome the hardships and challenges!]
I feel so blindsided.

2819
01:24:34,796 --> 01:24:35,716
Ugh!!!

2820
01:24:36,989 --> 01:24:38,931
[Who will seize
the chance for a status upgrade?]

2821
01:24:38,932 --> 01:24:41,064
[The next course is the ancient sites?]
Won't we do something while exploring the ancient sites?

2822
01:24:41,066 --> 01:24:42,604
[Bingo!]
Wow, wow!

2823
01:24:42,698 --> 01:24:44,257
[The Luxor Temple]
Now it really feels like I'm in Egypt!

2824
01:24:44,258 --> 01:24:45,310
I'm in Egypt!

2825
01:24:45,311 --> 01:24:46,103
Wow, seriously!

2826
01:24:46,104 --> 01:24:47,496
Wow, this is overwhelming.

2827
01:24:47,497 --> 01:24:48,716
It's truly mystical.

2828
01:24:48,717 --> 01:24:49,776
I'm kinda getting chills.

2829
01:24:49,777 --> 01:24:50,699
I'm getting goosebumps.

2830
01:24:50,700 --> 01:24:51,989
[And the status battle starts again]
Above the right eyebrow.

2831
01:24:51,989 --> 01:24:52,792
It's not.

2832
01:24:52,793 --> 01:24:53,893
Wow, I'm going crazy.

2833
01:24:53,894 --> 01:24:55,391
What could it be?
What's this, what's this?

2834
01:24:55,392 --> 01:24:57,399
[Oh…This… I know this…]

2835
01:24:57,400 --> 01:24:58,498
[I really want to be the prince]
Get it together!

2836
01:24:58,499 --> 01:25:00,025
Get it together! Get it together!

2837
01:25:00,026 --> 01:25:01,777
[No more pauper life!]
I've heard this! Oh, I'm going crazy!

2838
01:25:01,778 --> 01:25:03,065
Oh! Bread?

2839
01:25:03,066 --> 01:25:04,117
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

2840
01:25:04,925 --> 01:25:07,395
[An unpredictable battle to become a prince]
It's over, it's over!

2841
01:25:07,396 --> 01:25:09,714
I really want to do it.
This is driving me crazy!

2842
01:25:09,715 --> 01:25:10,698
[Who will become]
I am the prince!

2843
01:25:10,699 --> 01:25:13,799
[the 3rd princes?]
I am the prince!
